<h3 id=3D"output-to-a-handle">Output to a handle</h3>

<p>So far this writes output to a buffer and truncates when it runs out of
space. Usually we want this going to a sink, like a kernel object whether
that be a file, pipe, socket, etc. to which we have a handle like a file
descriptor. Instead of truncating, we <em>flush</em> the buffer to this sin=
k, at
which point there=E2=80=99s room for more output. The error flag is set if =
the
flush fails, but this is essentially the same concept as before.</p>

<p>In these examples I will use a file descriptor <code class=3D"language-p=
laintext highlighter-rouge">int</code>, but you can use
whatever sort of handle is appropriate. I=E2=80=99ll add an <code class=3D"=
language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">fd</code> field to the
buffer and a new constructor macro:</p>

<div class=3D"language-c highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre c=
lass=3D"highlight"><code><span class=3D"cp">#define MEMBUF(buf, cap) {buf, =
cap, 0, -1, 0}
#define FDBUF(fd, buf, cap) {buf, cap, 0, fd, 0}
</span>
<span class=3D"k">struct</span> <span class=3D"n">buf</span> <span class=3D=
"p">{</span>
    <span class=3D"kt">unsigned</span> <span class=3D"kt">char</span> <span=
 class=3D"o">*</span><span class=3D"n">buf</span><span class=3D"p">;</span>
    <span class=3D"kt">int</span> <span class=3D"n">cap</span><span class=
=3D"p">;</span>
    <span class=3D"kt">int</span> <span class=3D"n">len</span><span class=
=3D"p">;</span>
    <span class=3D"kt">int</span> <span class=3D"n">fd</span><span class=3D=
"p">;</span>
    <span class=3D"n">Bool</span> <span class=3D"n">error</span><span class=
=3D"p">;</span>
<span class=3D"p">};</span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<p>The buffered stream will be polymorphic: Output can go to a memory buffe=
