</span><span class=3D"o">-&gt;</span><span class=3D"n">len</span><span clas=
s=3D"p">);</span>
        <span class=3D"n">b</span><span class=3D"o">-&gt;</span><span class=
=3D"n">len</span> <span class=3D"o">=3D</span> <span class=3D"mi">0</span><=
span class=3D"p">;</span>
    <span class=3D"p">}</span>
<span class=3D"p">}</span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<p>I=E2=80=99ve arranged so that output stops when there=E2=80=99s an error=
. Also I=E2=80=99m using a
hypothetical <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">os_write<=
/code> in the platform layer as a full, unbuffered write.
Note that unix <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">write(2=
)</code> experiences partial writes and so must be used
in a loop. Win32 <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">Write=
File</code> doesn=E2=80=99t have partial writes, so on Windows an
<code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">os_write</code> could =
pass its arguments directly to the operating system.</p>

<p>The program will need to call <code class=3D"language-plaintext highligh=
ter-rouge">flush</code> directly when it=E2=80=99s done writing
